v1.0.54 build 59: delay onConfirmed after collapse animation

Root cause of collapse stutter: onConfirmed fires BEFORE the reverse
animation completes. The parent modal's setState triggers a full modal
rebuild during the 220ms collapse animation. Every animation frame
competes with the modal rebuild for the frame budget.

Fix: move onConfirmed call into the .then() callback of
_expandController.reverse(). Parent setState now fires ONCE after the
animation is complete and the picker is visually gone.

Also:
- Replaced AnimatedSize with manual AnimationController + ClipRect +
  Align(heightFactor: 0→1) from build 58. No per-frame parent layout.
- Dropped AnimatedRotation on chevron (static Icon). Eliminates second
  implicit ticker during expand/collapse.
- Removed Offstage/TickerMode pre-mount (caused stale state issues).
  Picker body conditionally rendered with `if (_expanded)`.
